<title>LITHUANIA: NEW CONSORTIUM FORMED FOR TELECOM BID.</title>
<headline>NEW CONSORTIUM FORMED FOR TELECOM BID.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuanian brokerage house Suprema said on Friday that a new consortium has been formed to bid in the tender to become a lead advisor in the privatisation of Lithuanian Telecom.</p>
<p>&quot;Banque Paribas, Suprema brokerage, Hermis Bank and Talinvest Ltd. announce a consortium to participate in the tender to draw up a privatisation program for Lithuanian Telecom,&quot; Suprema said in a statement.</p>
<p>The statement also said that the consortium is in negotiations with an auditor and another firm.</p>
<p>The Lithuanian government on Wednesday approved a short-list of ten foreign firms to bid for the tender.</p>
<p>The winner is expected to be announced at the end of June or the beginning of July.</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 22 35 17</p>
</text>
